en I will press the arrow again.\nTurn 24. TUTOR: It will give me something like this.\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 20 seconds]\nTurn 25. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - stops sharing screen] The tutor stops sharing their screen, and the view returns to the document with black lines drawn over it.\nTurn 25. TUTOR: Okay, perfect. Let me see if it came up on my end. Okay.\nTurn 26. TUTOR: So, your nickname is Blaze987654. Right?\nTurn 27. STUDENT: Yes.\nTurn 28. TUTOR: Perfect. Cool. So, let me... Yeah, it's a dog.\nTurn 29. TUTOR: [SCREEN_INTERACTION: tutor - sharing screen] The tutor shares their screen again, showing the an educational game platform lobby. The screen shows two players have joined: \"TK\" (tutor) and \"Blaze987654\" (student). The instructions on screen say \"Go to play.funquiz.com and enter Game ID: 5774064\".\nTurn 29. TUTOR: Are you ready to start the game?\nTurn 30. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 8 seconds]\nTurn 30. TUTOR: Are you ready to start the game?\nTurn 31. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds]\nTurn 31. TUTOR: Okay. Okay.\nTurn 32. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 3 seconds] Tutor clicks the \"Start\" button on the an educational game platform screen.\nTurn 32. TUTOR: Can we get started?\nTurn 33. STUDENT: Yes.\nTurn 34. TUTOR: Okay. Okay. And you have to answer every question in thirty seconds. So I'll also answer, you'll also answer, and then we will see who gets the most points.\nTurn 35. STUDENT: Okay.\n\nRespond as the TUTOR. Give only your response, no labels or prefixes.\n\nNEXT REPLY INSTRUCTION:\nProvide targeted scaffolding now. Identify the specific unresolved obstacle in the student's current mathematical work. Offer only the smallest useful hint, representation, or clarification that makes the next step accessible. Use the learner's actual numbers and ideas when available. Leave the key calculation or inference for the student and invite one manageable next step. Do not give a full solution, stack several leading questions, repeat an explanation the learner already understands, or invent unseen worksheet details.\nFor this next reply only, use the specified policy in context. Give the student one clear, manageable invitation to think. Be mathematically accurate and concise. Do not mention policy names, routing, evaluation, or these instructions.\n/no_think"
